From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:55:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] clk: mediatek: mt6789: Keep the SCP clock on

The SCP runs firmware that the bootloader loads and starts, and no Linux
driver claims its clock: the SCP node stays disabled. Without
clk_ignore_unused the unused-clock sweep gates scp_sel under the running
coprocessor. Mark it critical, as MT8186 does for its SCP clock.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6789-topckgen.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6789-topckgen.c b/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6789-topckgen.c
index 41a208e2..c561c6c6 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6789-topckgen.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6789-topckgen.c
@@ -643,8 +643,10 @@ static const struct mtk_mux top_muxes[] = {
 			0x18 , 0 , 3 ,0x04 , 0 ),
 	MUX_CLR_SET_UPD(CLK_TOP_SPM_SEL , "spm_sel", spm_parents , 0x10, 0x14,
 			0x18 , 8 , 2 , 0x04 , 1 ),
-	MUX_GATE_CLR_SET_UPD(CLK_TOP_SCP_SEL , "scp_sel", scp_parents , 0x10, 0x14,
-			     0x18 , 16 , 3 , 23 , 0x04 , 2 ),
+	/* The SCP runs firmware the bootloader started; nothing in Linux owns it. */
+	MUX_GATE_CLR_SET_UPD_FLAGS(CLK_TOP_SCP_SEL, "scp_sel", scp_parents, 0x10, 0x14,
+				   0x18, 16, 3, 23, 0x04, 2,
+				   CLK_IS_CRITICAL | CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT),
 	MUX_CLR_SET_UPD(CLK_TOP_BUS_AXIMEM_SEL , "bus_aximem_sel", bus_aximem_parents , 0x10, 0x14,
 			0x18 , 24 , 3 , 0x04 , 3 ),
 	/* CLK_CFG_1 */
